<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Burao</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Burao is a city in the Togdheer region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Somaliland</a>, on the seasonal Togdheer river. It was a seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habr-yunis">Habr Yunis</a> sultans and a centre of the Isaaq clans, and in May 1991 it hosted the conference at which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somali-national-movement">Somali National Movement</a> declared the restoration of Somaliland's independence. It is now one of Somaliland's largest cities and a major livestock market.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/burao.jpg" alt="Burao" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jethrostrong1 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Burao,_Somaliland.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
